ccomplished; 3. not derivable by inference.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "असिद्ध (II) m. one of the five fallacious hetus (in logic). It is of three kinds, viz., आश्रयसिद्ध, स्वरूपसिद्ध and व्याप्यतासिद्ध. The first consists in the पक्षत्व property not existing in the पक्ष, the second in the so-called ‘hetu’ not residing in the पक्ष and the third in the साध्यत्व property not residing in the साध्य.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["असिद्धं", "असिद्धः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["asidDaM", "asidDaH"]}, {"id": "asidDA", "headword": "असिद्धा", "headword_slp1": "asidDA", "fold": "asidDa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "असिद्ध (I) a. (f. द्धा) 1. Raw, unbaked; 2. unaccomplished; 3. not derivable by inference.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "asitangavina": [{"id": "ASitaMgavIna", "headword": "आशितंगवीन", "headword_slp1": "ASitaMgavIna", "fold": "asitangavina", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "आशितंगवीन a. formerly grazed by cattle.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आशितङ्गवीन", "आशितङ्गवीनं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ASitaNgavIna", "ASitaNgavInaM"]}], "asitanBava": [{"id": "ASitaMBava", "headword": "आशितंभव", "headword_slp1": "ASitaMBava", "fold": "asitanBava", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "आशितंभव n. 1. food; 2. satisfaction, satiety, e.g. फलैर्यष्वाशितंभवम्.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आशितम्भव", "आशितम्भवं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ASitamBava", "ASitamBavaM"]}], "asis": [{"id": "ASis", "headword": "आशिस्", "headword_slp1": "ASis", "fold": "asis", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "आशिस् f. 1. Prayer, wish; 2. blessing, benediction (it is thus defined- वात्सल्याद्यत्र मान्येन कनिष्ठस्याभिधीयते । इष्टावधारकं वाक्यमाशीः सा परिकीर्तिता ॥ आशिस् differs from वर in as much as it is a mere expression of good wishes which possibly may not come off true, while वर is a boon sure of fulfilment. Thus we have in Sak. व